y particular error, maybe starting with the metrics for media-mongodb makes sense. Alternatively, using get_traces for services that might be affected by media-mongodb\'s status. But first, confirming if media-mongodb is actually down via metrics would be the next step.\n</think>\n\nget_metrics  \n"up{job=\\"media-mongodb\\"}"  \nThe previous deployment check showed media-mongodb has 0/1 available replicas. To confirm if the service is actually down or just not reporting metrics, I need to query its Prometheus metrics directly. This will validate whether the service is unreachable, crashing, or simply not emitting metrics.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 410, 'prompt_tokens': 2462, 'total_tokens': 2872, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc7b-71ea-7e82-b797-c27cb499bd73-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2462, 'output_tokens': 410, 'total_tokens': 2872}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='e4f537a4-637c-4da3-a633-8541f4ee4429'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with their social network application, which consists of many microservices. They mentioned that some or none of the microservices might have faults. \n\nFirst, they started by using the get_services tool to list all services in Grafana, which gives an overview of the components. Then, they checked metrics for the user-service using get_metrics, but got an empty result, indicating possible issues. Next, they used kubectl to check deployments and found that media-mongodb has 0/1 available replicas, meaning it\'s not running as expected.\n\nNow, the user is focusing on media-mongodb. The next step is to check the metrics for media-mongodb directly using get_metrics with the query "up{job=\\"media-mongodb\\"}". The response will show if the service is up or down. If the metric is 0, it confirms the service isn\'t running. If there\'s no data, maybe the metrics aren\'t being collected properly. \n\nAfter getting the metrics, if media-mongodb is indeed down, they should check the pods associated with it. Using exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with "kubectl get pods -n social-network" can show if the pod is in a crash loop or has errors. If the pod is not running, checking the logs with "kubectl logs" might reveal the root cause, like configuration errors or dependency issues. \n\nThey should also look into the deployment configuration for media-mongodb to ensure the correct number of replicas and check for any rollout issues. If the problem persists, looking at the service\'s dependencies via get_dependency_graph could help identify if other services are affecting it. \n\nOverall, the key steps are verifying the service\'s status through metrics, checking pod health, reviewing deployment settings, and examining logs for detailed error messages. This approach should help pinpoint whether the issue is with the service itself, its configuration, or external factors.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"query": "up{job=\\"media-mongodb\\"}"}', 'name': 'get_metrics'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a8566f1f9e885cd5', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 422, 'prompt_tokens': 3437, 'total_tokens': 3859, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc7b-8560-74a0-a0a3-155099ee14f3-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_metrics', 'args': {'query':