f it doesn\'t, that\'s why the volume mount is failing. The tool to use here is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get configmap media-mongodb -n social-network". \n\nBy running this command, they can confirm whether the ConfigMap is present. If it\'s missing, that\'s the root cause. If it exists, maybe there\'s another issue. But given the error message, the ConfigMap isn\'t found, so creating it or checking its existence is crucial. This will help pinpoint the problem accurately.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl get configmap media-mongodb -n social-network"  \nThe pod\'s `FailedMount` event indicates the ConfigMap `media-mongodb` is missing. This command will confirm whether the ConfigMap exists in the namespace, directly addressing the root cause of the volume mounting failure preventing the container from starting.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=288, prompt_tokens=4937, total_tokens=5225, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc7c-33ae-7463-84b0-d460fdebc4fd-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4937, 'output_tokens': 288, 'total_tokens': 5225}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='58d9dac8-e82a-46e1-9845-e81a970b960b')]]
