od list directly will reveal its current status, including any errors or restarts, which is critical to diagnosing the root cause.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 336, 'prompt_tokens': 2636, 'total_tokens': 2972, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc7b-9a02-7842-9aa2-729e170a25eb-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2636, 'output_tokens': 336, 'total_tokens': 2972}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='5f0ef53a-5e53-4ce1-8cba-b44bc784e118'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the media-mongodb service in their social network application. From the previous steps, they checked the deployments and saw that media-mongodb has 0/1 available replicas. Then they queried Prometheus metrics for media-mongodb, but got an empty result, indicating that the service might not be up or not emitting metrics.\n\nNow, the user is suggesting to run "kubectl get pods -n social-network" again. Wait, they already did that earlier, and the output showed media-mongodb as 0/1. But maybe they want to check the pods again to see if there\'s any change or more details. However, the previous output didn\'t show the pod name, so maybe the pod isn\'t listed because it\'s in a crash loop or pending. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user wants to check the pod\'s logs to see why it\'s not running. But the available tool is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, which can run commands like logs. Wait, the user\'s last tool call was "kubectl get pods -n social-network", and the response included media-mongodb as 0/1. But the